{"case_id":"C035","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","configuration","input_semantics","attack_surface"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["ares_sconfig_append_fromstr","parse_nameserver_uri","ares_uri_parse_buf","ares_get_server_addr","ares_get_server_addr_uri"],"reason":"S1 adds a new nameserver configuration syntax and URI parser path that H0 cannot exercise. `ares_sconfig_append_fromstr` now tries `parse_nameserver_uri` before the legacy `parse_nameserver`, accepting `dns` URIs with host scope, UDP port, and the `tcpport` query key. H0 only calls `ares_create_query` or DNS message parsing/writing APIs, so it provides neither the configuration entry point nor the server state needed to reach these new semantics. This is commit-induced rather than merely historical because the URI path and distinct TCP/UDP-port serialization were introduced in S1.","evidence":["In S1, `ares_sconfig_append_fromstr` newly calls `parse_nameserver_uri(entry, &s)` and falls back to `parse_nameserver(entry, &s)` only if URI parsing fails.","The new `parse_nameserver_uri` calls `ares_uri_parse_buf`, requires scheme `dns`, parses an optional `%` interface scope, reads the URI port, and accepts the `tcpport` query key.","The new `ares_server_use_uri` selects URI output when `server->tcp_port != server->udp_port`, and `ares_get_server_addr` then calls `ares_get_server_addr_uri`.","`ares_get_server_addr_uri` serializes the server through `ares_uri_set_scheme`, `ares_uri_set_host`, `ares_uri_set_port`, `ares_uri_set_query_key`, and `ares_uri_write_buf`.","`test/ares-test-fuzz-name.c` only passes a null-terminated fuzz string to `ares_create_query`.","`test/ares-test-fuzz.c` only feeds bytes to `ares_dns_parse` and, after successful parsing, exercises DNS record accessors and `ares_dns_write`; it does not call `ares_sconfig_append_fromstr`, `ares_uri_parse_buf`, or `ares_get_server_addr`.","The list/array substitutions in `ares_search.c`, `ares_sysconfig_files.c`, `ares_buf.c`, and `ares_strsplit.c` are internal refactoring, but the newly accepted nameserver URI grammar is a distinct externally supplied configuration-input surface."],"recommended_action":"Add a fuzz target that passes arbitrary bounded strings to `ares_sconfig_append_fromstr` with both `ignore_invalid` modes and exercises server serialization through `ares_get_server_addr`, covering `dns://` authority parsing, IPv4/IPv6 hosts, `%` scopes, ports, `tcpport` query values, percent encoding, malformed delimiters, and parse/write round trips."}
